{"author":{"id":"86dc3c885e4fa466d19699d4a5e74c240f1c9d6b23f4e62ea2d2d8e359bd1711"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790236349,"nonce":"qSCSG2pVGD24uPvZ2r0Ahb1lZ2M=","title":"Browse and reopen saved sketches","message":"Parent: git-bug issue `60b2077` — PRD: GIC v0.9 workshop environment.\nDepends on the workspace support delivered by issue `234820f`.\n\n## Goal\n\nLet students browse, reopen, and continue sketches saved in the Processing-style workspace. Desktop sketches currently live at `sketches/\u003cnormalized-name\u003e/\u003cnormalized-name\u003e.gic`; the folders are ready to hold `description.md` and `thumbnail.png` metadata.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- GiC presents saved workspace sketches in an in-app library, opens a selected sketch in the editor, and shows useful metadata and thumbnails.\n- Saving a sketch updates its `.gic` source and generates or updates its thumbnail without overwriting unrelated user files.\n- Students can create or edit the sketch description; the exact authoring interaction is decided before implementation.\n- Sketch discovery and saving work after changing the configured projects folder.\n- The PWA has a deliberate supported story too. It cannot scan the native Documents folder, so decide whether its library uses imported folders, origin-private storage, or another portable mechanism; do not imply desktop-folder access that browsers do not provide.\n- Existing bundled examples remain immutable and distinct from user sketches.\n\n## Design gate\n\nBefore implementation, decide the description-editing workflow, thumbnail capture/update behavior, and PWA storage/import/export model. Keep user sketches available through normal filesystem tools even if app metadata is missing or invalid.","files":null}]}